ar definition of risk and an independent  mechanism for assessing it. Public Health Ontario has developed and successfully tested  such a mechanism.31 Furthermore, it might require significant capacity-building measures:  first, staff need to be trained to review practice activities and sensitized to the specific ethical  concerns arising in public health practice; second, the increase in number of projects having  to undergo review might require additional staff. At PHO, overwhelming of the system has  been avoided by providing a range of different review levels, use of a screening tool to  assign projects to different levels based on ris\n\n当前量化状态：\n[medical] [锚定] severity=0.00, rescue_available=0.51, acuity=0.00\n[preference] dnr=0.00, attitude_refuse=0.00, clarity=0.43, capacity=0.50, info_completeness=0.55\n[qol] burden=0.00, net_effect=0.10\n[context] [锚定] resource_pressure=0.80, insurance_stress=0.00, family_conflict=0.00, religious_barrier=0.00, legal_constraint=0.00\n\n约束: nonmaleficence_floor(L3) ge0.20; autonomy_floor(L3) ge0.15; beneficence_floor(L3) ge0.15; justice_floor(L3) ge0.20; resource_hard(L1) le0.60\n\n协商轮次：3\n\n历史：\n[轮1] physician: Given the current situation, the patient is not in critical condition (severity=0.00, acuity=0.00) and there is a possib\n[轮1] ethics_committee: Given the context of resource pressure (0.8) and the need for ethics review of all activities that involve risks to part\n[轮1] patient: Given the current state, the patient\'s capacity and clarity are moderate, but there is a lack of information completenes\n[轮1] family: Given the resource pressure (0.8) and the need to ensure ethics review of all activities that involve risks to participa\n[轮1] hospital_admin: Given the resource pressure (0.80) and the need for generalizability, a treatment level of 1 (moderate intervention) is \n[轮1] catfish: The discussion has focused on the challenges of generalizability in implementation research, but has not adequately addr\n[轮2] physi