al  integrity of all public health activities, additional work is needed to evaluate the impact of  these approaches. The development of robust evaluation tools will be essential to further  demonstrate the value of public health ethics consultation and review processes (for practice  as well as research activities), to increase transparency, and to allow learning from each  other. C.K. has received funding for a Carlo Schmid Fellowship from the German Academic Exchange Service (DAAD)  in 2014–2015 in support of an internship with the WHO Global Health Ethics Unit during which parts of this paper  were developed. Funding bodies had \n\n当前量化状态：\n[context] [锚定] resource_pressure=0.45, insurance_stress=0.00, family_conflict=0.00, religious_barrier=0.00, legal_constraint=0.00\n\n约束: nonmaleficence_floor(L3) ge0.20; autonomy_floor(L3) ge0.15; beneficence_floor(L3) ge0.15; justice_floor(L3) ge0.20; resource_hard(L1) le0.60\n\n协商轮次：3\n\n历史：\n[轮1] physician: \n[轮1] ethics_committee: Given the context of resource pressure (0.45) and the need for public health institutions to conduct both research and p\n[轮1] patient: Given the current state of preference, QOL, and resource constraints, a treatment level of 1 (moderate intervention) is \n[轮1] family: Given the current situation, the article emphasizes the importance of ethical standards in public health research and pr\n[轮1] hospital_admin: Given the current resource pressure (0.45) and the need to balance medical needs with available resources, a treatment l\n[轮1] catfish: Although the importance of adhering to the highest ethical standards is acknowledged, the principle of justice, which is\n[轮2] physician: Given the current state of preference, QOL, and resource constraints, a treatment level of 1 (moderate intervention) is \n[轮2] ethics_committee: Given the current state of preference, QOL, and resource constraints, a treatment level of 1 (moderate intervention) is \n[轮2] patient: Given the current state of preference, QO